WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.342
Before finishing the module use this slide as a
self-check You should be able to

00:00:05.355 --> 00:00:10.382
explain what a variable stores recognize the four
basic data types we used and trace

00:00:10.408 --> 00:00:16.074
a simple arithmetic calculation from the inputs to
the result You should also

00:00:16.101 --> 00:00:20.587
be able to explain why formatting matters and why
input sometimes needs to be converted

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:26.405
before we can use it numerically Try to answer these
questions in your own words

00:00:26.418 --> 00:00:31.460
rather than only remembering syntax If you can
explain what the code is doing and

00:00:31.486 --> 00:00:36.342
why you are in a good position to move forward If
one area still feels

00:00:36.368 --> 00:00:40.526
unclear return to the related runnable example and
change a few values
